ress"}],"gloss":"frontier fortress"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"pōla","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருங்கை","parts":[{"text":"பெருங்கை","lemma":"பெருங்கை","gloss":"great means"}],"gloss":"great means","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அற்ற","parts":[{"text":"அற்ற","lemma":"aṟutal","gloss":"lost"}],"gloss":"lost"},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"eṉ","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"புலம்பு","parts":[{"text":"புலம்பு","lemma":"pulampu","gloss":"loneliness"}],"gloss":"loneliness"},{"surface":"முந்துறத்தே","parts":[{"text":"முந்துறத்து","lemma":"muntuṟattu","gloss":"front yard"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"is in your front yard"}]}],"literal":"Without considering your greatness that protects mankind, / with the attitude devoid of virtue where love has vanished, / if people like you also are such, / may people like us not be born in this world indeed! / My beloved wife of faultless conduct, / if she possesses even a little life, / remaining without thinking of me is difficult indeed, therefore, / as the virtue-less god of death decides without justice, / \"Has he become a stranger? May my life perish!\" saying, / she of distress who laments and stays grieving many things, / to remove this state of my distressed wife, / I have departed, may you live long, Lord! Look there, / I will go with a sorrowful heart; those who are angry with you, / like their highly guarded frontier fortress, / my loneliness, which has lost great means, is in your front yard.","translation":"\"Without considering your own greatness in protecting mankind, if even people like you behave with such a virtue-less attitude, devoid of love, then may people like us never be born in this world! My beloved wife of faultless conduct, if she still has a little life left in her, cannot bear to live without thinking of me. Therefore, thinking, 'Has he become a stranger to me? May my life perish!' as the merciless god of death unjustly decides her fate, she lives in deep distress, lamenting and grieving over many things. To put an end to this miserable state of my wife, I am departing now. May you live long, O Lord! Look there—I go with a sorrowful heart, leaving my helpless loneliness, which has lost all support, right in your front yard, standing like the heavily guarded frontier fortress of your enemies.\"","modern":"\"மன்பதைக் காக்கும் உமது பெருமையை நோக்காமல், அன்பு நீங்கிய அறமற்ற பார்வையோடு நீங்களும் இப்படி நடந்து கொள்வீர்களானால், எங்களைப் போன்றவர்கள் இனி இவ்வுலகில் பிறக்காமல் இருக்கட்டும்! குற்றமற்ற கொள்கையுடைய என் அன்பான மனைவி, இன்னும் சிறிது உயிர் வைத்திருப்பாளானால், என்னை நினைக்காமல் இருப்பது அவளுக்கு அரிது. அதனால், 'அவர் எனக்கு அந்நியராகிவிட்டாரோ? என் உயிர் அழியட்டும்!' என்று அறமற்ற கூற்றுவன் நீதியின்றித் துணிய, அவள் பலவாறு வருந்தித் துயரத்தோடு வாழ்கிறாள். என் மனைவியின் இந்தத் துன்ப நிலையைத் தீர்ப்பதற்காக நான் இங்கிருந்து புறப்படுகிறேன். தலைவனே, நீ வாழ்க! இதோ பார், வருத்தமுற்ற நெஞ்சோடு நான் செல்கிறேன். உன்னைப் பகைத்தவர்களுடைய அரிய காவல் கொண்ட எல்லைக் கோட்டையைப் போல, பெருந்துணையற்ற என் வறுமை உனது முற்றத்திலேயே நிற்கிறது.\"","explanation":"The poet Peruṅkuṉṟūr Kiḻār addresses the Cēra king Cēramāṉ Kuṭakkōc Cēral Irumpoṟai after being kept waiting for gifts. Disappointed by the king's lack of generosity, the poet decides to leave empty-handed and expresses his deep sorrow. He describes his wife back home, who is suffering in extreme poverty and waiting in distress, fearing that he has abandoned her or died. The poet bids farewell to the king, stating that he is leaving with a heavy heart, but leaving his helpless poverty (pulampu) right at the king's doorstep. He compares this lingering poverty to the heavily guarded frontier fortress of the king's enemies, serving as a silent, powerful accusation against the king's neglect.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.2],[1.2,1.5],[1.5,1.6],[1.6,2.75],[2.75,2.98],[2.98,3.9],[3.9,4.4],[4.4,4.4]